---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = new Date('2026-11-19T12:00:00Z');
const contact = 'joshgrant+seedling@pm.me';
---
<Base title="Seedling Privacy Policy" description="How Seedling, the daily planner for iPhone and iPad, handles your data.">
  <article>
    <p class="mb-3 text-[15px] text-muted tabular-nums">
      Last updated <time datetime={updated.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}>November 19, 2026</time>
    </p>
    <h1 class="mb-8 text-[40px] leading-[1.12] font-semibold tracking-[-0.028em] text-balance">Seedling Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Seedling doesn’t collect your data. There are no accounts, ads, analytics or trackers, and I don’t run a
        server. What you write in Seedling stays on your devices and in your own iCloud.
      </p>

      <h2>What Seedling stores</h2>
      <p>
        Seedling stores your tasks, schedule, meals, notes, water, focus sessions and settings on your device.
        Widgets read the same data to show it on your Home Screen and Lock Screen.
      </p>

      <h2>iCloud</h2>
      <p>
        If you’re signed in to iCloud, Seedling syncs your data through your private iCloud database so it shows up
        on your other devices. Apple stores it, and I can’t see it. If iCloud isn’t available, your data stays on the
        device.
      </p>

      <h2>Apple Health</h2>
      <p>
        If you allow it, Seedling saves the water you log to Health. It also reads water from Health so your daily
        total includes water logged in other apps. Seedling asks the first time you log water.
      </p>
      <p>
        Water read from Health is only shown to you: Seedling never stores it, syncs it, shares it or uses it for
        advertising. You can change access at any time in the Health app or in Settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        Apple handles the Unlock Seedling purchase through the App Store. I never see your payment details. Seedling
        checks your purchase on your device.
      </p>

      <h2>Feedback</h2>
      <p>
        When you choose to send feedback, Seedling starts an email to me, and nothing is sent until you send it. If
        you use Apple Mail, the draft already includes the Seedling version, your device type (such as “iPhone”) and
        your iOS version, and you can see and edit all of it before sending. Other email apps start with just a
        subject line.
      </p>
      <p>I use your email address and message only to reply and to improve Seedling, and I never share them.</p>

      <h2>Notifications and alarms</h2>
      <p>
        Seedling uses local notifications only to update the app icon badge. It uses alarms only to tell you when a
        focus session or break ends. Both are created on your device, and nothing is sent to me.
      </p>

      <h2>Upgrading from Seedling 1</h2>
      <p>When you update, Seedling copies your existing data into the new version on your device.</p>

      <h2>Your data, your choice</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Export everything from Seedling’s Settings.</li>
        <li>Delete entries in the app, or delete the app to remove its data from that device.</li>
        <li>Delete the iCloud copy in Settings › [your name] › iCloud by managing your storage.</li>
        <li>Delete water saved to Health in the Health app.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Seedling doesn’t collect personal information from anyone, children included.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, I’ll update this page and the date at the top.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
